Carafe bench: a sampler heap index that NAK assembles from bytes. For DXVK 3.x's D3D9 shaders NAK loads the
16-bit index from the push data as two bytes and joins them with BitFieldInsert:
umin(bfi(bfi(bfi(bfi(0, bfe(c0[push], 0, 8), 0, 8), bfe(c0[push], 8, 8), 8, 8), 0, 16, 8), 0, 24, 8), 0x7ff).
The texture pass did not know this form, took the push data word itself as the handle's low half and the
texture descriptor's word as its high half, so nearly every draw of the game read an empty TIC slot and
sampled black. A chain of BitFieldInsert whose fields are contiguous bytes of one constant buffer word, with
zeros above them, now tracks as a bit field of that word, like a BitFieldUExtract.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/texture_pass.cpp
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/texture_pass.cpp
@@ -373,6 +373,96 @@
